	(text "M3J1: SCK to GND selects the PCM5102A's internal PLL\n(BCK = 32 or 64 fs, 32 to 384 kHz). BCK and LCK on\nconsecutive GPIOs (46, 47): one PIO side-set drives both.\nVIN from VIN (after D1): the breakout has its own two\nregulators, it is not on the module's 3V3. Pin 1 = SCK.\nM3J2: nine unconnected holes (pin 1 = FLT, at the SCK\ncorner); they only hold the board, whose jack end is\n30 mm from the 6-pin row. AGND is not grounded here.\nGeometry: board 31.6 x 17.0 mm; the 6-pin row 1.5 mm\nfrom the short edge; the 9-pin row 1.5 mm from the long\nedge next to the SCK pin, its first hole (FLT) 6.35 mm\nalong the board from the 6-pin row and 0.635 mm outside\nthe SCK hole; the jack on the opposite long edge at the\nfar end, 1.5 mm proud.\nStrap bridges on its underside as usually delivered:\nFLT low, DEMP low, XSMT high, FMT low. I2S needs the B0\nmodule (GPIO47), enabled only after a PSRAM probe\nhas found none."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 381 259.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
